      "path": "eslint.config.js",
      "content": "The following `wordingRules` entry replaces `no-restricted-syntax` for non-test UI files with options that include only the identity and wording selectors. Consequently, `npm run lint` accepts a direct `date \u003e instrument.expiration` comparison in most of `src/ui`, despite the new restriction applying there. Compose the expiration selectors into that entry as well (while retaining its wording selectors and exemptions).",
      "existing_code": "  ...expirationExemptRules,",
      "start_line": 23,
      "end_line": 23,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "eslint.deps.config.js",
      "content": "Checking only the immediate operand misses expiration members wrapped in TypeScript assertions or optional chains. For example, `date \u003e (instrument.expiration as string)` passes because the right operand is a `TSAsExpression`; conversely, `a.expiration \u003c (b.expiration as string)` is incorrectly rejected even though both sides are expirations. Look through expression wrappers on both sides when detecting expiration members and applying the two-expiration exemption, and add coverage for wrapped operands.",
      "existing_code": "    selector: `${relational}[left.property.name='expiration']:not([right.property.name='expiration'])`,",
      "start_line": 21,
      "end_line": 21,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "eslint.deps.config.js",
      "content": "The selectors do not distinguish computed properties from dot access. `date \u003e instrument['expiration']` is accepted because the property's AST node has `value`, not `name`, while `date \u003e dates[expiration]` is rejected even when `expiration` is a variable containing another key. Handle static computed string keys explicitly and require `computed=false` for identifier property names, applying the same checks to the two-expiration exemption.",
      "existing_code": "selector: `${relational}[left.property.name='expiration']:not([right.property.name='expiration'])`,",
      "start_line": 21,
      "end_line": 21,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
